{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"Validation passes cleanly (`valid=True`, no diagnostics) after the second iteration. The deliverable is complete.\n\n{\"submission\":\"submission.json\",\"summary\":\"First partial-but-usable audit map (map.json) for the hashicorp/raft snapshot (commit c0dc6a0b), submitted as a `research` product alongside 33 cited source ranges.\\n\\nWhat it records:\\n- A1 (formation/advancement): pre-vote campaign (preElectSelf, no term change) -> real vote campaign (electSelf, persists term + self-vote) -> per-term vote grants (requestVote/requestPreVote with leader-stickiness, membership, log-up-to-date and one-vote guards) -> leader no-op + replication -> commitment matches advance commitIndex only at/above startIndex (first entry of the leader's own term).\\n- A2 (context/authority): durable current term + per-term vote, setState clearing the known leader, step-down-and-bump on newer terms, and leadership transfer via TimeoutNow with the candidateFromLeadershipTransfer exemption (no pre-vote, no equal-term step-down).\\n- The sourced connection between them: formation eligibility and the commitment quorum are read from the latest configuration; config changes open only when latest==committed and the leader has committed an entry in its own term (configurationChangeChIfStable); old work is bounded by present authority (votes honoured only for their term, handleStaleTerm/step-down on newer-term replies, truncation rolling latest back to committed, inflight futures failed with ErrLeadershipLost on step-down).\\n\\nExplicitly retained rather than smoothed over: 4 local anomalies in core_overview.open_details (appendEntries StoreLogs-failure TODO at raft.go:1541; electSelf returning a nil response channel on self-vote persistence failure at raft.go:2023; checkLeaderLease nil-replState assumption at raft.go:1054; 'unexpected command' treated as a granted pre-vote), and 8 unmapped Surfaces headed by the h